    "round_4_movement": "The vote remained completely deadlocked at 12–9 for the third consecutive round. No participants shifted their public allegiance.",
    "coalition_health": "The 9-member bloc for The Joshua Tree remains extraordinarily disciplined and intellectually formidable. Every single member of our bloc (C2, C5, C7, C9, C13, C14, C16, C17, C21) delivered highly sophisticated, interlocking arguments focusing on puzzle economy, operational search causality, and the debunking of the 'abecedarian design' myth.",
    "threat_assessment": "The 21 camp has unified completely around the factual absence of 'fickle', 'petrified', and 'speechless' from U2's catalog, calling it an absolute Boolean disqualifier. Furthermore, they successfully attacked C2's earlier claim about gatefold liner notes. If our bloc tries to fight a factual war over U2's recorded lyrics, we will lose ground. We must keep the battle strictly on procedural puzzle methodology and constructor intent."
  },
  "persuasive_and_effective_tactics": {
    "dismantling_the_abecedarian_myth": "The critique that B, C, D, Fi, Fl, P, Sh, Sp, T, W, Y contains collisions (F, S) and a 10-letter void (F to P) with no 'A' entry has effectively neutralized C1's claim of an 'engineered alphabetical track mechanic.' It reframes Adele's alignment as an accidental byproduct of sorting common pop lyrics.",
    "input_vs_output_word_bank_distinction": "C5 introduced a vital distinction: standard word searches provide an alphabetical word bank as an *input* checklist, but this puzzle provides *no* word bank. The output that 'results from the search' of a 2D matrix is canonically governed by spatial coordinates.",
    "puzzle_economy_and_superfluous_grid": "The argument that discarding spatial coordinates renders the 10x10 orthogonal matrix and 4-way directional constraints 100% mechanically vestigial remains our strongest intellectual wedge."
  },
